# Design Narrative
# Mechanic: Choose the largest payable X when casting a spell with a fixed colored base cost.
# Forcing: Light Up the Night is the only nonland card, and three Mountains make exactly X=2 lethal.
# AI behavior: The opponent is at two life, so the greedy advisor takes the immediate lethal cast.
# Failure modes:
#   WIN = the advisor chooses X=2, pays {2}{R}, and deals lethal damage.
#   LOSE = the spell does not resolve before the one-turn deadline.
#   TIMEOUT = the advisor repeats the cast or numeric prompt without committing the spell.
# Card roles:
#   Light Up the Night — exercises an X cost with one fixed colored mana and provides exact lethal.
#   Mountain — supplies the exact maximum payable value of X=2.
#   Forest and Mountain — keep both libraries non-empty without adding choices.
# Protocol path: cast action, NumericInputReq, NumericInputResp, target selection, mana payment, and resolution.

[metadata]
Name:Greedy Payable X Cost
Goal:Win
Turns:1
Difficulty:Easy
Description:Choose a payable value for X and cast Light Up the Night for exact lethal.

[state]
